# Project purpose

Maintain Holler as reusable React 19 and Mantine 8 components and layouts.
The destination React app will supply AWS data and application behavior later.
Next.js is the current preview host. Supabase adapters and archived auth source
are retained for reference, not dependencies of the portable UI.

# Source boundaries

- `src/ui/index.ts` defines the presentation-only public API.
- `src/features/` groups feature views, display types, and connected preview wrappers.
- `src/components/` holds shared components and preview navigation/modals.
- `src/styles/` holds the theme, CSS Modules declarations, and shared styles.
- `src/app/` contains thin Next routes and preview runtime composition.
- `src/lib/services/` and `src/lib/navigation/` support connected preview wrappers.
- `src/lib/adapters/` contains fixture services and retained Next/Supabase implementations.
- `src/ui/connected.ts` and `_legacy_auth/` are excluded from the public handoff.

# Portable components

Accept data, request state, and controlled values through typed props. Report user
actions through callbacks. Keep only visual state locally. Do not import Next,
backend/auth SDKs, application contexts, service/navigation providers, or fixtures
into the exported dependency graph. The host owns fetching, routing, auth, caching,
and persistence. No AWS service or router needs to be selected for the UI package.

Keep preview wrappers separate from presentation views. Retained server actions
belong in the adapter layer, not feature component directories. Default routes `/`
and `/dashboard` show transactions with local data and no sign-in requirement.
Do not present simulated workflow outcomes as confirmed backend operations.

# Styling and types

Use Mantine props and CSS Modules. Reuse `src/styles/theme.ts` (exported as
`hollerTheme`) and `src/ui/styles.css`. Merge theme/PostCSS settings with the host.
Use explicit TypeScript interfaces rather than `any`; exported display models
must not depend on a backend schema or generated SDK types.

# Workflow

Read the relevant source and docs before editing. Keep components focused and
preserve unrelated changes. Do not modify hosted services, database schemas, or
archived authentication unless the task requires it.

Use `src/features/FEATURE_README_TEMPLATE.md` for feature documentation. Update
`docs/react-integration.md` when public exports change; `docs/ui-decoupling.md`
describes the connected preview only.

Run checks appropriate to the change: `npm run typecheck`, `npm run check:ui`,
`npm run test:react-handoff`, `npm run test:portability`, and `npm run lint`.
`npm run export:react` generates the ignored `build/react-ui/` handoff. Browser
layout/interaction checks and real AWS integration checks remain separate from
render tests. Do not commit generated output or credentials.
